    <title>Useful</title>
    <updated>2026-10-17T09:10:14Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" href="https://positivitybriefing.com/#item-1" type="text/html"/>
    <content type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Many public libraries lend more than books: some offer museum passes, tools or seed packets. Check your branch’s catalogue before buying something you’ll use only once.</div>
    </content>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>https://positivitybriefing.com/feed.atom#979d060a68fd473d019f2ccfc0bbd54f5c41ccc8e2a040a0f2a4e880c86e22f5</id>
    <title>Hopeful</title>
    <updated>2026-10-17T09:10:14Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" href="https://positivitybriefing.com/#item-2" type="text/html"/>
    <content type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">A shared tool cupboard in a block of flats can turn an awkward repair into a neighbourly exchange: one drill, kept in good order, serves many homes.</div>
    </content>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>https://positivitybriefing.com/feed.atom#610a8370ad71123936721de04113e642329252a078bbec635fa958ba86e2e15b</id>
    <title>Action</title>
    <updated>2026-10-17T09:10:14Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" href="https://positivitybriefing.com/#item-3" type="text/html"/>
    <content type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Spend three minutes watching a patch of ground for ants; notice where they travel and whether they carry anything, without disturbing their route.</div>
    </content>
  </entry>
